n_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[],"frozen_at":1791816598,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-12T14:49:58Z","frozen_sha":"423f24f71d09f349b8ce5769b537eb4d4800ad35","head_ref":"copilot/make-semantic-convention-selection-instance-scoped","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":38265751582},"loop_kind":"pr_conflict_resolver","merge_base_sha":"2ac45ba9fd68877bd1474847803119bdb14bac7e","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nMake RPC and service-peer semantic convention selection instance-scoped, so separately configured `OpenTelemetry` instances can emit different conventions in the same JVM.\n\nFor 3.0, remove global-backed RPC factories and the no-argument RPC/service-peer selection helpers. Pass the instrumentation's `OpenTelemetry` instance instead:\n\n```diff\n-RpcClientMetrics.get()\n+RpcClientMetrics.get(openTelemetry)\n-RpcSpanNameExtractor.create(getter)\n+RpcSpanNameExtractor.create(getter, openTelemetry)\n-SemconvStability.emitOldRpcSemconv()\n+SemconvStability.emitOldRpcSemconv(openTelemetry)\n```\n\nThe client/server attribute extractors, server metrics, dual-emission context customizer, remaining RPC/service-peer selection helpers, and `rpcSchemaUrl` likewise require an explicit instance.\n\nRPC consumers pass their own instance, and AWS RPC extractors are instance-owned. Span names, attributes, metrics, and schema URLs follow the same selection. Legacy child metrics no longer inherit a dual-emitting parent's method.\n\nDatabase, messaging, and code conventions remain unchanged.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes #20135","title":"Make semantic convention selection OpenTelemetry instance-scoped"},"mode":"publish","pr":20474,"pr_author_id":